  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Acute viral upper respiratory infection (J06.9)</content>. A common cold: sore throat, runny nose, and cough with a low-grade fever after exposure to students with colds. No features of streptococcal pharyngitis, sinusitis, or pneumonia. He is 50 with no chronic heart or lung disease, so a positive influenza or COVID-19 test would not change treatment. ACP and CDC advise against antibiotics for the common cold. [S]<list><item>No antibiotic and no testing.</item><item>Acetaminophen 500 mg to 1 g every 6 hours as needed, no more than 3 g a day.</item><item>Avoid combination cold medicines: dextromethorphan with sertraline can cause serotonin toxicity, and the night-time products contain sedating antihistamines that undo his sleep plan; honey and warm drinks for the cough.</item><item>Return for breathlessness, chest pain, fever above 38.5 C after three days, or symptoms beyond ten days.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Major depressive disorder (F32.2)</content>. One week of sertraline 50 mg; mild early nausea has settled. No suicidal thoughts or thoughts of harming others. [S]<list><item>Continue sertraline 50 mg each morning.</item><item>Cognitive behavioral therapy continues; first session held last week.</item><item>Safety plan, 988 Suicide &amp; Crisis Lifeline, and clinic number confirmed.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Chronic insomnia comorbid with depression (G47.00)</content>. About four and a half hours of sleep a night; keeping the sleep rules. [S]<list><item>No sedating cold remedies; keep the fixed rising time while unwell.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Guideline basis: VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Major Depressive Disorder (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); Management of Chronic Insomnia Disorder in Adults: A Clinical Practice Guideline From the American College of Physicians (2016); Appropriate Antibiotic Use for Acute Respiratory Tract Infection in Adults: Advice for High-Value Care From the American College of Physicians and the Centers for Disease Control and Prevention (2016)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Preventive visit next week as booked; sooner for the warning signs above. Next scheduled visit 2026-10-22: preventive health visit at 50. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
